From 550c00ed1c8c126a292a7e007e470024b681840c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:36:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chat): unclip expanded tool detail inside tool strip body

Clicking a running tool item toggled the expanded state, but the detail
section never became visible: .tool-call-item kept flex:1 1 0 (flex-basis
0 + flex-shrink 1) inside the column .tool-strip-body, so the expanded
item was compressed back to ~26px, and .tool-strip-body's max-height:
180px clipped whatever remained.

- .tool-call-item.expanded: flex:0 0 auto (flex:none) so the item grows
  to its content height and cannot be shrunk by the flex container
- .tool-strip-body:has(.tool-call-item.expanded): max-height:none so an
  expanded detail is fully visible (the args <pre> still scrolls at
  200px internally)
---
 packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
index 416f7710a..6a697b47d 100644
--- a/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
+++ b/packages/client/src/components/hermes/chat/MessageList.vue
@@ -2048,6 +2048,12 @@ defineExpose({
   &::-webkit-scrollbar {
     display: none;
   }
+
+  // When any tool item is expanded to review its arguments, let the body
+  // grow past the compact 180px cap so the detail section is fully visible.
+  &:has(.tool-call-item.expanded) {
+    max-height: none;
+  }
 }
 
 .tool-strip-pending {
@@ -2098,6 +2104,7 @@ defineExpose({
   }
 
   &.expanded {
+    flex: 0 0 auto;
     align-items: flex-start;
     height: auto;
     min-height: 26px;
-- 
2.53.0

